  "id": "psychological-intervention",
  "term": "psychological intervention",
  "definition": "A psychological intervention is a psychological or social approach used to help people, rather than a purely medical procedure. It can be delivered by many kinds of helpers, including mental health professionals, other health workers, caregivers, peers, religious leaders, or automated formats such as internet, audio, or video programs, and these options may be combined.",
